HEAD is now at 195b908 chore: claim T-004
=== launching claude for T-003 ===
T-003 is built, all four checks pass, and the branch `agent/T-003` is pushed (commit `8cf0723`). I didn't open a PR: you asked me only to push, and `run-task.sh` opens the PR itself. Six small changes fall outside the task's `Touches:` paths, so the auto-merge will route this to human review instead of merging it.

**Changes outside `Touches:`** (the feature can't run without them):
- `apps/api/src/app.module.ts`: one line to register the new metrics module with the API.
- `packages/calculations/src/index.ts` and `packages/connectors/src/index.ts`: one export line each so the API can use the new code.
- `apps/api/package.json` and `pnpm-lock.yaml`: the API now depends on `@pactlab/calculations`.

**Acceptance criteria**
- **HealthyCo** reconciles exactly: billing supports ARR of USD 402,840.00, the same as the management figure. No finding is raised.
- **TroubledCo**: management reports ARR of USD 1,450,000 but billing supports only USD 176,118.71. This produces a CRITICAL draft finding. Every citation in it resolves through the evidence lineage endpoint (tested). The gap breaks down as void invoices (USD 720,000 a year), uncollectible invoices (USD 300,000 a year) and a USD 150,000 one-time charge.
- **Reviewer approval**: only a deal lead or reviewer can approve, and a note is required. Approving twice records it once. If the evidence changed after the page loaded, the API refuses (409), and an earlier approval then shows as stale.
- **Access**: target-side contributors get 403 and other tenants get 404.

**Commands run**
- `pnpm lint`: passed, 15/15 tasks.
- `pnpm typecheck`: passed, 15/15 tasks.
- `pnpm test`: passed. New tests are calculations 27, connectors 12 (6 new), API 27 (7 new metrics end-to-end tests) and web 8 (3 new).
- `pnpm test:fixtures`: passed, 8/8, including running the seed twice with the new billing and FX data.
- `next build` with `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_ORIGIN` set: passed, `/metrics` and `/metrics/[dealId]` compile. Without those variables it fails on the home page because they aren't set.
- `prettier --check`: my files pass. Three files I didn't touch already fail it (`money.ts`, `contract.ts`, `testing.ts`).

**Unfinished or needing a decision**
- **No table for reconciliations or approvals.** Adding one means changing `packages/db`, which is outside this task. Approvals are stored as audit and outbox events instead. That only holds if outbox events are never deleted, so a proper `metric_reconciliations` table should be a follow-up task.
- **Draft findings aren't saved as findings yet.** They are sent as `finding.draft_proposed` events for the findings work in T-004 to pick up.
- **The Stripe adapter isn't selectable as a connection provider yet.** That needs a change in `apps/api/src/connections/adapter-registry.ts`, outside scope. For now, `pnpm seed` loads the Stripe-style data through the existing CSV connection, and the metrics read it the same way whichever connection it came from.
- **Already-seeded databases won't pick up the new billing data.** The seed's sync run uses a fixed key (`seed:<company>:v1`) and already counts as complete there. A fresh database is fine.
- **The UI can't approve anything yet.** Web sign-in isn't wired, so `/metrics` shows the signed-out state, the same as the existing deal pages. I also had to add a second copy of the existing placeholder sign-in token stub in `metrics/_lib/api.ts`, and both copies need replacing when sign-in lands.
- **No sidebar link to Metrics**, because `apps/web/lib/navigation.ts` is outside scope.
- **The FX rates are synthetic, not real ECB rates**, and the fixture READMEs say so.
- **Exchange-rate movements show up as expansion or contraction** in the month-to-month MRR breakdown rather than as their own line; this is documented in the formula text.
